MODIFIED BY PROJECT SNIPER
--------------------------
patches.json holds exact byte patches. Each patch replaces a span of an
upstream file with new text; that text contains portions of the original
upstream code together with Project Sniper's changes. native_runtime.py
applies the patches to a COPY of the installed package's dist/ directory under
templates/motion/.sniper-native-runtime/<identity>/hyperframes/; the installed
package in templates/motion/node_modules/hyperframes is never changed.

The following upstream files were modified by Project Sniper (September 2026):

  dist/cli.js                      28 patches (runtime realm checks, file-backed
                                   frame transport, zero-anchored source
                                   extraction clock, half-open video windows,
                                   sequential source work). In the adapted
                                   runtime this patched file is renamed
                                   dist/native-render-sdk.mjs.
  dist/hyperframe.runtime.iife.js  2 patches (same-document realm checks)
  dist/hyperframe-runtime.js       2 patches (same content as the file above)
  dist/hyperframe.manifest.json    1 patch  (records the patched runtime hash)
  dist/native-capture-library.mjs  new file derived from the patched
                                   dist/cli.js (1 patch: library entry instead
                                   of the command-line entry point)
  dist/studio/assets/index-CfQexXc6.js
                                   3 patches (Studio page analytics off: the
                                   analytics project key is replaced, so the
                                   page's own "key configured" check fails and
                                   no usage events are sent)
  dist/studio/index.js             3 patches (the same change in the Studio
                                   library entry)

Added by Project Sniper (not upstream code): dist/cli.js in the adapted runtime
is replaced by a three-line wrapper written by native_runtime.py;
frame-source-transport.mjs and native-export-guard.mjs are Project Sniper
files copied into the adapted runtime's dist/.

WHY THE NOTICE IS NOT INSIDE THE PATCHED FILES
----------------------------------------------
native_runtime.py verifies the SHA-256 of every adapted file against
patches.json before the runtime is used, and the runtime identity is a hash of
patches.json. Writing a notice into the patched bytes would change those
hashes and invalidate the qualification of the adapted runtime. This NOTICE,
shipped beside patches.json, is the modification notice for those files; the
adapted runtime directory also carries SNIPER-RUNTIME.json, the patch manifest
that lists every modified file and its hashes.

